 "stage": 13.97, "flow": 5260, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "2006-11-24T18:00:00Z", "stage": 17.08, "flow": 10900, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "2006-09-03T01:30:00Z", "stage": 18.8, "flow": 15599, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "2005-10-10T11:45:00Z", "stage": 13.71, "flow": 4991, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1999-09-18T00:00:00Z", "stage": 23.51, "flow": 0, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1996-09-08T00:00:00Z", "stage": 16.3, "flow": 9710, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1992-08-20T00:00:00Z", "stage": 16.59, "flow": 10400, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1962-07-07T00:00:00Z", "stage": 20.16, "flow": 20400, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1960-08-01T00:00:00Z", "stage": 16.21, "flow": 0, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1955-09-22T00:00:00Z", "stage": 17.97, "flow": 15200, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1942-10-16T00:00:00Z", "stage": 16.74, "flow": 11000, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1928-09-01T00:00:00Z", "stage": 21.8, "flow": 0, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}, {"occurredTime": "1908-08-01T00:00:00Z", "stage": 22.6, "flow": 0, "preliminary": "O", "olddatum": false}]}, "lowWaters": {"historic": [{"occurredTime": "1994-06-08T00:00:00Z", "stage": 1, "flow": -9999, "statement": ""}, {"occurredTime": "1995-10-13T00:00:00Z", "stage": 1.13, "flow": -9999, "statement": ""}, {"occurredTime": "1996-10-04T00:00:00Z", "stage": 1.54, "flow": -9999, "statement": ""}]}, "impacts": [{"stage": 25, "statement": "Historic and catastrophic flooding across Duplin county, comparable to the flood following Hurricane Florence. Numerous communities cut off, and travel is next to impossible. Countless homes and businesses are flooded across the county. In the River Landing community near Wallace, devastating flooding is expected with over half of the homes significantly inundated."}, {"stage": 22, "statement": "Devastating flooding across most of the county. Travel is nearly impossible with numerous roads countywide impassable or washed out. Many homes across the county are inundated. In the River Landing community near Wallace, several homes are likely inundated, with numerous residences surrounded by water or have water up to their foundations."}, {"stage": 20, "statement": "Widespread flooding across much of the county. Many roads flooded and impassable including Highways 41 and 50 and Interstate 40. Numerous homes and communities near the river are surrounded by water, with several likely inundated. In the River Landing community near Wallace, several homes close to the river are likely surrounded by water."}, {"stage": 18, "statement": "Numerous roads flooded, and some homes and businesses are likely inundated. Water floods Highways 41 and 50, and parts of Interstate 40. Areas many miles from the river are flooded due to tributaries backing up. Water threatens homes and buildings in the River Landing community near Wallace."}, {"stage": 16, "statement": "Many secondary roads are flooded. Water affects Highways 41 and 50 and travel delays are likely. Areas many miles from the river are affected as small streams backup and flood. Muddy Creek, Cypress Creek, and Island Creek flood areas around Chinquapin."}, {"stage": 15, "statement": "Secondary roads adjacent to the river flood and may be impassable. Tributaries that drain into the river flood secondary roads. Water surrounds homes and properties in the River Landing community in Wallace."}, {"stage": 13, "statement": "Low land flooding adjacent to the river and its tributaries is expected. River access docks are impacted as well."}]}, "images": {"probability": {"weekint": {"stage": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/CHIN7.SSTG.prob.weekint.gif", "flow": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/CHIN7.QINE.prob.weekint.gif", "volume": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/CHIN7.volume.prob.weekint.gif"}, "entperiod": {"stage": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/CHIN7.SSTG.exceed.90day.gif", "flow": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/CHIN7.QINE.exceed.90day.gif", "volume": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/CHIN7.volume.exceed.90day.gif"}, "shortrange": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/short_term/CHIN7.shortrange.hefs.png"}, "hydrograph": {"default": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/hydrographs/chin7_hg.png", "floodcat": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/hydrographs/chin7_record.png"}, "photos": []}, "dataAttribution": [{"abbrev": "US Geological Survey", "text": "USGS--Water Resources of the United States", "title": "US Geological Survey", "url": "https://waterdata.usgs.gov/nwis"}, {"abbrev": "USGS", "text": "02108000", "title": "Observations courtesy of U.S. Geological Survey", "url": "https://waterdata.usgs.gov/nwis/inventory/?site_no=02108000"}], "impactsLowWaters": [], "normalThreshold": {"value": 0, "units": "ft"}, "hydronotes": [], "datums": {"vertical": {"value": [{"label": "National Geodetic Vertical Datum of 1929", "abbrev": "NGVD29", "description": "A fixed reference adopted as a standard geodetic datum for elevations determined by leveling. The datum was derived for surveys from a general adjustment of the first-order leveling nets of both the United States and Canada. In the adjustment, mean sea level was held fixed as observed at 21 tide stations in the United States and 5 in Canada. The year indicates the time of the general adjustment. A synonym for Sea-level Datum of 1929. The geodetic datum is fixed and does not take into account the changing stands of sea level. Because there are many variables affecting sea level, and because the geodetic datum represents a best fit over a broad area, the relationship between the geodetic datum and local mean sea level is not consistent from one location to another in either time or space. For this reason, the National Geodetic Vertical Datum should not be confused with mean sea level. See North American Vertical Datum of 1988 (NAVD 88). NGVD 29 should not be used as Mean Sea Level. NGVD 29 is no longer supported by NGS.", "value": 17.28}, {"label": "North American Vertical Datum of 1988", "abbrev": "NAVD88", "description": "A fixed reference for elevations determined by geodetic leveling. The datum was derived from a general adjustment of the first-order terrestrial leveling nets of the United States, Canada, and Mexico. In the adjustment, only the height of the primary tidal bench mark, referenced to the International Great Lakes Datum of 1985 (IGLD 85) local mean sea level height value, at Father Point, Rimouski, Quebec, Canada was held fixed, thus providing minimum constraint. NAVD 88 and IGLD 85 are identical. However, NAVD 88 bench mark values are given in Helmert orthometric height units while IGLD 85 values are in dynamic heights. See International Great Lakes Datum of 1985, National Geodetic Vertical Datum of 1929, and geopotential difference. NAVD 88 should not be used as Mean Sea Level.", "value": 16.3}]}, "horizontal": {"value": []}, "notes": {"value": []}}, "inundation": {"enabled": true, "url": "https://mapservices.weather.noaa.gov/static/rest/services/NWS_FIM/FIM_chin7/MapServer", "zeroDatum": {"value": 16.319, "datum": "NAVD88"}, "downloads": {"depthGrids": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/downloads/fim/chin7/chin7_shapefiles.zip", "images": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/downloads/fim/chin7/chin7_images.zip", "kmz": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/downloads/fim/chin7/chin7_kmz.zip"}, "siteSpecificInfo": "", "dataAttribution": [{"text": "USGS", "title": "Observations courtesy of the US Geological Survey", "url": "", "image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/fim/"}, {"text": "State", "title": "NC 